# {{ title }}

YAMD tracks assignments and coursework deadlines without a separate calendar app.
Everything lives in the notes themselves — `course:` front matter groups them,
`due:` dates mark when things are due, and the dashboard brings it all together.

::toc{depth=2}

---

## Naming a course

Add `course:` to the front matter of any note. Notes in the same course are
grouped together in the dashboard and when generating a cheat sheet.

```yamd
---
title: Binary search trees
course: CS201
due: 2026-11-01
---
```

The `due:` key here marks the **whole note** as a submission (an essay, a lab
report, a problem set). The extension picks it up automatically.

---

## Marking a note as reviewed

Add `reviewed:` with today's date to tell the dashboard you've looked at this note recently. Notes without a recent review date appear in the **Stale topics** list after `yamd.study.staleAfterDays` days (default 14).

```yamd
---
title: Sorting algorithms
course: CS201
reviewed: 2026-10-17
---
```

---

## Task-level deadlines

Any task item in a note can carry `{due=YYYY-MM-DD}`. These show up in the
agenda alongside note-level due dates.

- [ ] Read chapters 4–6 {due=2026-10-24}
- [ ] Submit lab report 2 {due=2026-11-01}
- [ ] Revise for midterm {due=2026-11-08}
- [x] Complete tutorial 3 {due=2026-10-10}

---

## The dashboard

Run **YAMD: Open Study Dashboard** from the command palette. The dashboard shows:

### Agenda

Deadlines grouped by urgency:

| Section | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- |
| **Overdue** | Past due and not done |
| **Today** | Due today |
| **This week** | Due in the next 7 days |
| **Later** | Further out |
| **Done** | Completed items |

Each item shows the note title, the due date, how far away it is ("in 3 days",
"yesterday") and the course. Click any item to jump to that note.

### Course progress

A progress bar per course showing how many tasks are done vs total.
Courses with no tasks still appear if any note carries that `course:` label.

### Stale topics

Notes in a course not opened or reviewed in the last `yamd.study.staleAfterDays`
days, sorted oldest first. A prompt to revisit them.

### Study heatmap

A GitHub-style 26-week heatmap of your study sessions (logged by the timer).
Each cell's colour intensity corresponds to minutes studied that day.
Hover a cell to see the exact date and minutes.

### Review queue

How many flashcards are due for review today. Click **Review now** to open the
review panel.

---

## Settings

| Setting | Default | Meaning |
| ------- | ------- | ------- |
| `yamd.study.staleAfterDays` | `14` | Days before a topic is flagged as stale |

---

## Example: a module overview note

Here is what a typical course overview note looks like. It gives the dashboard
everything it needs.

```yamd
---
title: CS201 overview
course: CS201
reviewed: 2026-10-17
lang: en
---

# CS201 overview

## Deadlines

- [ ] Problem set 1 {due=2026-10-24}
- [ ] Midterm exam {due=2026-11-08}
- [ ] Lab report 2 {due=2026-11-01}
- [ ] Problem set 2 {due=2026-11-15}
- [ ] Final exam {due=2026-12-10}

## Topics

- [x] Arrays and sorting
- [x] Recursion and recurrences
- [ ] Trees and BSTs
- [ ] Hash tables
- [ ] Graphs and BFS/DFS
```
